// Two echoes over two chasms; one seed at your feet, one up a staircase of blocks past an ember.
name Echo
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hint A stranger law: a cell lives when its neighbour count is odd. One seed is at your feet; the other is up the blocks on the far side, where an ember paces. Two stones wait in two chasms.
tip Grow the first echo to cross, fetch the high seed, plant the second stone, rewind, then grow both from solid rock. An echo is a cross with a broken ring around it.
intro Deeper in, the law is stranger. What lived here echoed, and the echoes left stairs. The seeds were scattered: one near, one high.
outro An echo is the shape of its source, repeated and thinned. You are learning the grammar.
